  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n   We will optimize the step function representation using multiple restarts with the COBYLA local optimizer. The central idea is to represent the function as a length-80 vector with 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 and integral=40, and minimize the maximum overlap. This approach focuses on:\n   - Using the provided initial solution as a starting point\n   - Perturbing the solution and using projected gradients in regions of interest\n   - Balancing between local refinement and global exploration\n   \n   The algorithm leverages the structure of the problem to explore promising regions near the parent solution while maintaining feasibility. Non-convexity is addressed through multiple restarts and projection-based feasibility maintenance.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n   Representation: h \u2208 \u211d^{80} with:\n     - Lower bounds: h[i] \u2265 0 for all i\n     - Upper bounds: h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n     - Equality constraint: \u2211_{i=1}^{80} h[i] = 40\n   Objective (to minimize): \n     C5 = max_{k} [ (np.correlate(h, 1-h, 'full')) * dx ]\n     where dx = 2.0/80\n   Constraints handling: \n     Feasibility restoration: \n        clip(x, 0, 1) for all i, then normalize sum to 40 (except when integral<8, we refill)\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n   - Initialize with parent solution validation\n   - Generate perturbations: random jittering and heuristic shifts in key regions\n   - For each candidate:\n        1. Feasibility projection (clip and normalize)\n        2. Objective calculation (correlation and maximum extraction)\n        3. COBYLA optimization with bounds and equality constraint\n   - Track best solution (lowest C5)\n   - Failure recovery: if local optimization stuck, expand search\n\n4. Search choices\n   - Basis: local COBYLA optimization (200 iterations)\n   - Perturbations: \u00b14% Gaussian noise and structure-preserving shifts\n   - Key regions targeted: \n        - High-value zones from parent\n        - Endpoints (0 and 2)\n        - Jump boundaries (0.3 and 1.7)\n\n5. Numerical robustness\n   Memory: 80 variables requires ~500 MB using 64-bit floats\n   Feasibility check: after every 5 iterations, restore with projection\n   Fallback: if optimization stumbles, use grid search on parent's peaks\n\n6. Runtime safeguards\n   Time tracking: 1100s budget with 10% overhead per iteration\n   Solution storage: \n        best_x = None\n        best_c5 = float('inf')\n   Evaluation loop:\n        for restart in range(n_restarts):\n            if time_remaining > 5 s:\n                run 1 COBYLA call\n                update best solution",
